So, the solutions (rounded to the nearest integer) are $x={42}^{∘},{138}^{∘}.$" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278101 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278102 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278103 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278104 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278105 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1041 "selection" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278101 13194139534126 true] [17592186278100 1110 #uuid "b06000d4-cd35-503a-910d-7b21a3172aae" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278101 1034 "x={42}^{∘},{138}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278101 1111 #uuid "322f1808-370e-599c-854f-a59f96fec337" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278102 1034 "x={28}^{∘},{132}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278102 1111 #uuid "64b89554-fb75-51cc-b307-823fa7b33e83" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278103 1034 "x={32}^{∘},{128}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278103 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278103 1111 #uuid "0eb6a9c9-dcb6-59d4-b6da-dc83c86cfed6" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278104 1034 "x={52}^{∘},{138}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278104 1111 #uuid "81b425dd-bd8d-5863-aaa6-2aefe9adee1a" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278105 1034 "x={42}^{∘},{158}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278105 1111 #uuid "9b1fa623-b950-5f80-8cbd-9ba9ed3d620f" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278106 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278107 13194139534126 true] [17592186278106 1089 "q-120866" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278106 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534126 true] [17592186278106 1100 "Solve the equation $\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278106 1113 #uuid "49d94093-5a76-5a48-9933-3ad26a6829ff" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278106 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ 1 & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)={90}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${90}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={90}^{∘}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its maximum values at:\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\n$$\n\nSince the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is one period, and we have already found one maximum value in this period, we conclude that $x={90}^{∘}$ is the only solution." 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278108 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278109 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278110 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278111 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278112 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1041 "selection" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278109 13194139534126 true] [17592186278107 1110 #uuid "e451ba94-f8ea-5321-ab3f-a13fc9a3fc14" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278108 1034 "x={180}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278108 1111 #uuid "293e029f-767f-54c3-a403-dcd4fc60238d" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278109 1034 "x={90}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278109 1111 #uuid "cdebb2e3-f88b-5c18-ba79-e5686a1fd339" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278110 1034 "x={270}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278110 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278110 1111 #uuid "231ec4a1-9496-51e1-80f1-49e777b3d092" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278111 1034 "x={60}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278111 1111 #uuid "50be34b5-4fce-54c9-a3ce-1d702298b875" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278112 1034 "x={45}^{∘}" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278112 1111 #uuid "9abf62cf-85c4-52ed-a6e8-daa30ed11128" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278113 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278114 13194139534126 true] [17592186278113 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278117 13194139534126 true] [17592186278113 1089 "q-332216" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278113 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534126 true] [17592186278113 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-0.7,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$   are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$, $\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278113 1113 #uuid "abb3e962-4f1e-5cbf-bc32-5a4e2bf1bf6d" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278113 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-0.7)=-44.427\\,004{…}^{∘}≈-{44.4270}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-{44.4270}^{∘}$ is not in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ To get the first solution that's within the required domain, we need to find an angle that's coterminal with $-{44.4270}^{∘}.$ To do this, we simply add ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{44.4270}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={315.5730}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={44.4270}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={44.4270}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977985/assets/f3d2d41e1a58dd562ed47ae7e5fcdc79382c426700f520a1153111bfcf2d734b.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{44.4270}^{∘} \\\\  & ={224.4270}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈{224.4}^{∘},\\,x≈{315.6}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278115 13194139534126 true] [17592186278114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278116 13194139534126 true] [17592186278114 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534126 true] [17592186278114 1041 "field-1" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278114 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278116 13194139534126 true] [17592186278114 1110 #uuid "d51ba88d-3984-5504-b2bb-1fb572037baa" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278115 1034 "44.4" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278115 1111 #uuid "b95adefa-7f9b-5fbd-9348-57914717722c" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278116 1034 "224.4" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278116 1111 #uuid "483206c2-f753-5306-a63d-6718303e5bd4" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278118 13194139534126 true] [17592186278117 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534126 true] [17592186278117 1041 "field-2" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278117 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278118 13194139534126 true] [17592186278117 1110 #uuid "fb7b8933-68f8-597e-90ad-b6bda4d254a2" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278118 1034 "315.6" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534126 true] [17592186278118 1111 #uuid "91ddd2ef-0b80-558d-83db-c280a121d555" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278119 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278120 13194139534126 true] [17592186278119 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278122 13194139534126 true] [17592186278119 1089 "q-336283" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278119 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534126 true] [17592186278119 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-0.6,$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘},$ are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$, $\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278119 1113 #uuid "0cf4768e-f324-53aa-93ec-e41e3ef947d4" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278119 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-0.6)=-36.869\\,897…≈-36.8699\n$$\n\nSince $-{36.8699}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{36.8699}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={36.8699}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={36.8699}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977985/assets/8d88b4ccfe08c26c9d56effaf651e04703995ffaec4b7ab08187f62ddd1897de.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{36.8699}^{∘} \\\\  & ={216.8699}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-{360}^{∘} & ={216.8699}^{∘}-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & =-{143.1301}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈-{143.1}^{∘},\\,x≈-{36.9}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534126 true] [17592186278120 1000 #